## PR: New Project Wizard (Modal Stepper)
Title
- feat(project-wizard): Add New Project multi-step modal wizard

Problem / Context
- The current "Create New Project" is a simple AlertDialog that only captures a name. We need a low-friction, mobile-first wizard that lets users choose project type, add a cover, pick a template, optionally invite collaborators, and optionally enable auditions/AI—so creators can get started with the right defaults in under 60 seconds.

What this PR does
- Adds a ModalBottomSheet-based, 3-step new project wizard:
  1. Choose type (Story / Script / Comic / Game / Other)
  2. Title + short pitch + optional cover image
  3. Template selection + toggles (Enable Auditions, Enable AI) + optional invite flow
- Integrates with existing Project model creation path and shows a preview before finalizing.

Files (suggested)
- Add new file: `app/src/main/java/com/example/theforge/ui/NewProjectWizard.kt`
- Update: `app/src/main/java/com/example/theforge/MainActivity.kt` to trigger sheet from FAB
- Minor: `app/src/main/java/com/example/theforge/models/ProjectModels.kt` (if you extract models)

Testing / QA
1. Tap FAB or "Create New Project" -> wizard opens.
2. Step through 3 steps; test skip/finish early behavior.
3. Create project with cover upload and verify banner appears on ProjectLanding.
4. Create with "Enable Auditions" and check the Auditions tab exists on the new project.
5. Invite collaborator via the invite input and verify they appear in collaborators list.

Design brief for Gemini (visuals)
- Show a tall mobile sheet with three horizontally-swipable steps. Include:
  - Step 1: grid of large type cards with icons
  - Step 2: text fields (Title, Pitch), cover image placeholder with drop-in
  - Step 3: templates carousel + toggles + invite input
- Use brand accent (teal/indigo) + white cards + rounded corners. Provide 1–2 mockups: compact and expanded preview.

Labels / Reviewers
- labels: enhancement, ui, onboarding
- reviewers: @Kiyoshiakira, @mobile-dev
- Notes: add analytics events for step completion

