## PR: Auditions Data Models + Auditions Tab (Initial)
Title
- feat(auditions): Add CastingCall and AuditionSubmission models + Auditions tab

Problem / Context
- Auditions are core to the product but missing. We need data models and a basic UI to list and create Casting Calls attached to a project.

What this PR does
- Adds new models:
  - `CastingCall` (role, description, excerpt link, deadline, isOpen, submissions)
  - `AuditionSubmission` (submitter, mediaUri, notes, rating)
- Adds an Auditions tab to ProjectLandingScreen with a simple list of CastingCall cards and a "New Casting Call" sheet.

Files (suggested)
- `app/src/main/java/com/example/theforge/models/Auditions.kt` (new)
- `app/src/main/java/com/example/theforge/ui/AuditionsScreen.kt` (new)
- `MainActivity.kt` update: add Auditions tab handling

Small snippet (copyable)
```kotlin
data class CastingCall(
  val id: String = java.util.UUID.randomUUID().toString(),
  val role: String,
  val description: String,
  val excerptTabTitle: String? = null,
  val deadlineMillis: Long? = null,
  var isOpen: Boolean = true,
  val submissions: MutableList<AuditionSubmission> = mutableStateListOf()
)

data class AuditionSubmission(
  val id: String = java.util.UUID.randomUUID().toString(),
  val submitter: User,
  val mediaUri: Uri?,
  val notes: String,
  var rating: Int? = null,
  val timestamp: Long = System.currentTimeMillis()
)
```

Testing / QA
1. Open Project -> Auditions tab shows zero state with CTA.
2. Create a casting call with role, description, and optional excerpt.
3. Verify the new card appears and the "Open / Close" status toggles.
4. Submit a fake audition (mediaUri can be null for testing) and see it listed.

Design brief for Gemini
- Render a Project Auditions tab with a list of cards. Show "New Casting Call" modal with role, description, excerpt attach (dropdown of project tabs), deadline picker, and toggles (open/public). Include a submission list mockup and a submission card with small video thumbnail + short notes.

